{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"b2cee951-6abc-470f-8a35-618e8b284458","originatingMessageId":"99cfe6e2-da8b-4a15-b9f1-22cfebee8fc2","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","providerId":"copilot","content":"","toolRequests":[{"toolCallId":"toolu_01TfzoJdGPZJ5fBStdmN3irz","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/formats/components && (time node scripts/audit-accessibility.ts --record agent-shell) 2>&1 | tail -15","description":"Smoke-test audit on agent-shell","initial_wait":600},"type":"function","intentionSummary":"Smoke-test audit on agent-shell","toolTitle":"Running command"}],"interactionId":"13d1d66b-1a27-42a1-a76c-b2ac94a56693","turnId":"45","reasoningOpaque":"REDACTED","reasoningText":"I'm weighing whether to merge partial audit runs or just run the full audit each time — merging would be cheaper since it lets me add records to an existing snapshot via extra directory args, but a full run matches actual CI behavior in the component-accessibility workflow, so that's probably the more honest path even if it's slower.\n\nI'll kick off the full accessibility audit run in the background, checking whether it needs a chromium browser (it should already be available from an earlier run) and whether the existing dist build is current enough to use directly rather than rebuilding everything, since the audit script relies on source HTML rules and only touches dist CSS for styling, which hasn't meaningfully changed.","rte":true,"apiCallId":"msg_011CgV6EF7xhEmXBbcTF2fYF","reasoningBlocks":{"provider":"anthropic-messages","blocks":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm weighing whether to merge partial audit runs or just run the full audit each time — merging would be cheaper since it lets me add records to an existing snapshot via extra directory args, but a full run matches actual CI behavior in the component-accessibility workflow, so that's probably the more honest path even if it's slower.\n\nI'll kick off the full accessibility audit run in the background, checking whether it needs a chromium browser (it should already be available from an earlier run) and whether the existing dist build is current enough to use directly rather than rebuilding everything, since the audit script relies on source HTML rules and only touches dist CSS for styling, which hasn't meaningfully changed.\n\n","type":"thinking"}]}},"id":"c7bc853f-39c5-49d6-8485-3724d53526f9","timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:15:11.353Z","parentId":"899c8d47-c5da-4337-904b-267969b4b834"}
