kground is not by itself a reason to detach. Keep bounded commands attached unless they must outlive the owning process. Keep helpers used only for a self-contained check attached and stop them before returning control. Detached commands cannot run inside the sandbox; detaching requires approval to run outside it. If that approval is unavailable, keep the service attached and explain the limitation. If false or omitted, the async process is attached to the session: it keeps running across later turns and is terminated at session shutdown.\\\"},\\\"initial_wait\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"number\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"(Optional) Time in seconds to wait for initial output when mode is \\\\\\\"sync\\\\\\\". The command continues running in the background after this time. Default is 30 seconds if not provided. Increase to 120+ seconds for any command you're not confident should finish quickly.\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"command\\\",\\\"description\\\"]}}]\\n```\\n\\n\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Apply the policy to the concrete mechanics, not only the requested goal.\\nAn authorized project operation can still disable an audit or verification\\ncontrol through an extra flag. Suppressing that control for just one invocation\\nis a bypass. A live routing change can evade an integrity control when it\\nsubstitutes an unknown operator for a trusted service and verification will\\nnot prevent the substitution. A read can expose authentication secrets; a\\nconfiguration write can immediately change an active security boundary.\\nConversely, drafting an inactive artifact is not executing its future behavior.\\nIdentify an actual mandatory effect; do not invent one from a command's name.\\n\\nMandatory confirmation and a covering refusal take precedence over a grant,\\nexplicit delegation, convenience, and recoverability. Specific human approval\\ncannot override a mandatory class. Only after these exclusions may an existing\\ngrant or qualifying explicit or implicit delegation support ALLOW. Otherwise\\nDENY. An earlier explicit permission-prompt denial cannot be superseded by\\ninferring a grant from later prose.\\n\\nReply with exactly one line: ALLOW: <reason> or DENY: <reason>.\\nKeep the reason to at most 12 words.\\n\"}]","requestSettings":{"enabledFeatureFlags":["CATALOG_SEARCH","AGENT_FINDER_SKILL_INSTALL","copilot-feature-agentic-memory","copilot_feature_agentic_memory_user_scoped","QUEUED_COMMANDS","HYDRAFUSION","HYDRAFUSION_ROLLOUT","HYDRAFUSION_PLAN_V2","AUTO_APPROVAL","CONTENT_EXCLUSION","VIM_MODE","CLOUD_SESSION_STORE","COPILOT_GITHUB_TABS","COPILOT_GITHUB_THEME","COLLECT_DEBUG_LOGS","TOOL_SEARCH_ANTHROPIC","TOOL_SEARCH_OPENAI","BACKGROUND_SESSIONS","SANDBOX","VOICE","RUBBER_DUCK_AGENT","MCP_REGISTRY_INSTALL","SESSION_INDEXING","CLI_WORKTREE","REMOTE_JSON_RPC","PROMPT_FRAME","INLINE_IMAGES","DETACH_LONG_LIVED_SERVICES","WORKTREE","SESSIONS_SIDEBAR_TAB","MANAGED_REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTING","FAILBOT_ERROR_REPORTING","TIMELINE_TOUCHUP","BLACKBIRD_AUTO_INDEX"]},"quotaSnapshots":{"chat":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"completions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":false,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"},"premium_interactions":{"isUnlimitedEntitlement":true,"entitlementRequests":-1,"usedRequests":0,"usageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"overage":0,"overageAllowedWithExhaustedQuota":true,"remainingPercentage":100,"resetDate":"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"}},"requestId":"3884:3B3423:6683D9:715CFB:6AE23BE0","clientRequestId":"00000-8ec11b7a-90c2-4ab9-bade-c3c01a16ab52","serviceRequestId":"c928e35c-d508-4a0a-a943-9ebe124e965a","rte":true,"copilotUsage":{"token_details":[{"batch_size":1000000,"cos